%% ---- The reporting pass (llmdetailed §10.5.1) ------------------------------
%%
%% What the derived pack already gives this model without being asked: a
%% register per entity, a breakdown per %%enum-bound column, created-per-month,
%% a lifecycle report over all eleven state machines in the diagram's own order,
%% totals over the numeric columns, and children-per-parent for all 31
%% relationships. None of that needed anyone who understands how a school runs.
%%
%% These do. Each of the eight roles on the %%rbac matrix above is walked through
%% the four questions — what they open first, what tells them something is wrong
%% today, what they are asked for weekly, and what rots silently if nobody
%% looks — so each can do its whole job from what it can see.

%% -- principal: whether the school is working --------------------------------
    %%report principal-roll-by-year title: The roll, by year group entity: Student chart: bar x: year_group y: students help: The first number the head is asked for by governors and by the local authority, and the one every capacity decision starts from. Enrolled only — on leave and suspended students hold a place but are not in a classroom. sql: SELECT s.year_group, COUNT(*) AS students FROM bus_student s WHERE s.deleted_at IS NULL AND s.status = 'enrolled' GROUP BY s.year_group ORDER BY s.year_group
    %%report principal-attendance-by-year title: Attendance against the statutory floor entity: Enrollment chart: bar x: year_group y: attendance_pct help: The number an inspection opens with. Below ninety-five percent a year group is a conversation with the local authority, and the head would rather have it before they do. sql: SELECT s.year_group, ROUND(AVG(e.attendance_rate), 1) AS attendance_pct, COUNT(DISTINCT s.id) AS students FROM bus_enrollment e JOIN bus_student s ON s.id::text = e.student_id WHERE e.deleted_at IS NULL AND s.deleted_at IS NULL AND e.status = 'enrolled' GROUP BY s.year_group ORDER BY s.year_group
    %%report principal-open-serious-incidents title: Serious conduct still open entity: DisciplineIncident help: What would make the head say someone needs to fix this today. A serious or critical incident with no outcome recorded is a family waiting for an answer and a governing body that will ask for the file. sql: SELECT i.reference, s.first_name || ' ' || s.last_name AS student, i.category, i.severity, i.status, i.occurred_at, EXTRACT(DAY FROM now() - i.occurred_at)::int AS days_open FROM bus_discipline_incident i JOIN bus_student s ON s.id::text = i.student_id WHERE i.deleted_at IS NULL AND i.severity IN ('serious', 'critical') AND i.status NOT IN ('closed', 'dismissed') ORDER BY i.occurred_at
    %%report principal-fee-collection-by-term title: Billed against collected, by term entity: FeeInvoice chart: bar x: term y: collected help: The weekly question from the bursar in one row per term. Billed is what the school committed to teach for; collected is what actually arrived, and the gap is the working-capital conversation. sql: SELECT t.name AS term, SUM(f.total_amount) AS billed, SUM(f.amount_paid) AS collected, SUM(f.balance_due) AS outstanding FROM bus_fee_invoice f JOIN bus_academic_term t ON t.id::text = f.academic_term_id WHERE f.deleted_at IS NULL AND f.status <> 'cancelled' GROUP BY t.id, t.name, t.starts_on ORDER BY t.starts_on DESC
    %%report principal-oversubscribed-sections title: Groups holding more students than places entity: ClassSection help: A group over its capacity is a health-and-safety exposure and a teaching problem, and neither is visible from the timetable. Counted from the enrolments themselves rather than from the maintained counter, so a broken counter cannot hide it. sql: SELECT sec.code AS section, c.name AS course, st.first_name || ' ' || st.last_name AS teacher, sec.capacity, COUNT(e.id) AS enrolled FROM bus_class_section sec JOIN bus_course c ON c.id::text = sec.course_id LEFT JOIN bus_staff st ON st.id::text = sec.staff_id LEFT JOIN bus_enrollment e ON e.class_section_id = sec.id::text AND e.deleted_at IS NULL AND e.status = 'enrolled' WHERE sec.deleted_at IS NULL AND sec.status IN ('open', 'in_progress') GROUP BY sec.id, sec.code, c.name, st.first_name, st.last_name, sec.capacity HAVING COUNT(e.id) > sec.capacity ORDER BY COUNT(e.id) - sec.capacity DESC
    %%report principal-teaching-cover-gap title: Groups whose teacher has left or is on leave entity: ClassSection help: The report that rots silently. A teacher leaves, their sections keep their name on them, and nobody notices until a class turns up to an empty room. sql: SELECT sec.code AS section, c.name AS course, st.first_name || ' ' || st.last_name AS teacher, st.status AS teacher_status, t.name AS term FROM bus_class_section sec JOIN bus_staff st ON st.id::text = sec.staff_id JOIN bus_course c ON c.id::text = sec.course_id JOIN bus_academic_term t ON t.id::text = sec.academic_term_id WHERE sec.deleted_at IS NULL AND st.deleted_at IS NULL AND sec.status IN ('planned', 'open', 'in_progress') AND st.status <> 'active' ORDER BY t.starts_on, sec.code

%% -- registrar: every student in a group that exists -------------------------
    %%report registrar-unplaced-enrolments title: Enrolment requests not yet placed entity: Enrollment help: The registrar's queue, and the first screen of the day. A request left pending is a student with a free period and a family who thinks the subject was chosen. sql: SELECT s.student_number, s.first_name || ' ' || s.last_name AS student, c.name AS course, sec.code AS section, e.created_at FROM bus_enrollment e JOIN bus_student s ON s.id::text = e.student_id JOIN bus_class_section sec ON sec.id::text = e.class_section_id JOIN bus_course c ON c.id::text = sec.course_id WHERE e.deleted_at IS NULL AND e.status = 'pending' ORDER BY e.created_at
    %%report registrar-timetable-clashes title: Students booked into two groups at once entity: Enrollment help: What makes a registrar say that is wrong, someone needs to fix it today. Two enrolments in the same term on the same day and period means a child cannot attend one of them, and the first anyone hears of it is usually a missing mark. sql: SELECT s.student_number, s.first_name || ' ' || s.last_name AS student, a.code AS section_one, b.code AS section_two, a.day_of_week, a.period FROM bus_enrollment ea JOIN bus_enrollment eb ON eb.student_id = ea.student_id AND eb.id > ea.id AND eb.deleted_at IS NULL AND eb.status = 'enrolled' JOIN bus_class_section a ON a.id::text = ea.class_section_id JOIN bus_class_section b ON b.id::text = eb.class_section_id AND b.academic_term_id = a.academic_term_id AND b.day_of_week = a.day_of_week AND b.period = a.period JOIN bus_student s ON s.id::text = ea.student_id WHERE ea.deleted_at IS NULL AND ea.status = 'enrolled' AND a.deleted_at IS NULL AND b.deleted_at IS NULL ORDER BY s.last_name, a.day_of_week, a.period
    %%report registrar-section-fill title: How full each group is entity: ClassSection chart: bar x: section y: fill_pct help: What to open before agreeing to another enrolment, and what tells a head of department that a group is not viable. Places taken against places built, for the groups currently teaching. sql: SELECT sec.code AS section, c.name AS course, sec.capacity, COUNT(e.id) AS enrolled, ROUND(100.0 * COUNT(e.id) / NULLIF(sec.capacity, 0)) AS fill_pct FROM bus_class_section sec JOIN bus_course c ON c.id::text = sec.course_id LEFT JOIN bus_enrollment e ON e.class_section_id = sec.id::text AND e.deleted_at IS NULL AND e.status = 'enrolled' WHERE sec.deleted_at IS NULL AND sec.status IN ('open', 'in_progress') GROUP BY sec.id, sec.code, c.name, sec.capacity ORDER BY fill_pct
    %%report registrar-students-without-a-timetable title: Enrolled students in no group at all entity: Student help: A student on the roll with no enrolment anywhere is either a registration that never finished or a leaver nobody recorded. Both are invisible from every other screen and both cost the school money. sql: SELECT s.student_number, s.first_name || ' ' || s.last_name AS student, s.year_group, s.enrolled_on FROM bus_student s LEFT JOIN bus_enrollment e ON e.student_id = s.id::text AND e.deleted_at IS NULL AND e.status IN ('pending', 'enrolled') WHERE s.deleted_at IS NULL AND s.status = 'enrolled' GROUP BY s.id, s.student_number, s.first_name, s.last_name, s.year_group, s.enrolled_on HAVING COUNT(e.id) = 0 ORDER BY s.year_group, s.last_name
    %%report registrar-counter-disagrees title: Groups whose enrolled counter is wrong entity: ClassSection help: The maintained counter on a section is what every timetable row shows; when it disagrees with the enrolments themselves a hook has failed silently, and every screen has been lying since. Nothing else in the application notices. sql: SELECT sec.code AS section, sec.enrolled_count AS counter, COUNT(e.id) AS actual FROM bus_class_section sec LEFT JOIN bus_enrollment e ON e.class_section_id = sec.id::text AND e.deleted_at IS NULL AND e.status = 'enrolled' WHERE sec.deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY sec.id, sec.code, sec.enrolled_count HAVING sec.enrolled_count <> COUNT(e.id) ORDER BY ABS(sec.enrolled_count - COUNT(e.id)) DESC
    %%report registrar-withdrawals-this-term title: Students who left a group, and why entity: Enrollment help: What the registrar is asked for at every curriculum meeting. Read together the reasons say whether a subject is losing students to a clash, to difficulty, or to a teacher. sql: SELECT s.student_number, s.first_name || ' ' || s.last_name AS student, c.name AS course, e.withdrawn_on, e.withdrawal_reason FROM bus_enrollment e JOIN bus_student s ON s.id::text = e.student_id JOIN bus_class_section sec ON sec.id::text = e.class_section_id JOIN bus_course c ON c.id::text = sec.course_id WHERE e.deleted_at IS NULL AND e.status = 'withdrawn' AND e.withdrawn_on > now()::date - 120 ORDER BY e.withdrawn_on DESC

%% -- teacher: the room they are about to walk into ---------------------------
    %%report teacher-today title: Today's sessions, by teacher entity: ClassSession help: The first screen of a teaching day: what is on, where, and how many are expected. The room comes from the session where a one-off move was made and from the section otherwise, which is exactly the case a teacher needs told. sql: SELECT COALESCE(cover.first_name || ' ' || cover.last_name, st.first_name || ' ' || st.last_name) AS teacher, c.name AS course, sec.code AS section, COALESCE(sr.code, r.code) AS room, ses.starts_at, COUNT(e.id) AS expected FROM bus_class_session ses JOIN bus_class_section sec ON sec.id::text = ses.class_section_id JOIN bus_course c ON c.id::text = sec.course_id JOIN bus_staff st ON st.id::text = sec.staff_id LEFT JOIN bus_staff cover ON cover.id::text = ses.staff_id LEFT JOIN bus_room r ON r.id::text = sec.room_id LEFT JOIN bus_room sr ON sr.id::text = ses.room_id LEFT JOIN bus_enrollment e ON e.class_section_id = sec.id::text AND e.deleted_at IS NULL AND e.status = 'enrolled' WHERE ses.deleted_at IS NULL AND ses.status = 'scheduled' AND ses.starts_at >= date_trunc('day', now()) AND ses.starts_at < date_trunc('day', now()) + interval '1 day' GROUP BY cover.first_name, cover.last_name, st.first_name, st.last_name, c.name, sec.code, sr.code, r.code, ses.starts_at ORDER BY ses.starts_at
    %%report teacher-registers-not-taken title: Sessions that ran with no register entity: ClassSession help: A missing register is a hole in the statutory return, and it is invisible the moment the day ends. Chased the same week it is a reminder; chased at the end of term it is a compliance finding nobody can now fix. sql: SELECT st.first_name || ' ' || st.last_name AS teacher, c.name AS course, sec.code AS section, ses.starts_at FROM bus_class_session ses JOIN bus_class_section sec ON sec.id::text = ses.class_section_id JOIN bus_course c ON c.id::text = sec.course_id LEFT JOIN bus_staff st ON st.id::text = COALESCE(ses.staff_id, sec.staff_id) WHERE ses.deleted_at IS NULL AND ses.status <> 'cancelled' AND ses.register_taken = false AND ses.ends_at < now() ORDER BY ses.starts_at
    %%report teacher-marking-outstanding title: Work handed in and not yet marked entity: Assessment help: What a teacher opens to plan an evening. Submitted results with no mark, oldest paper first, because a class waiting three weeks for a grade has stopped acting on the feedback. sql: SELECT c.name AS course, sec.code AS section, a.title, a.due_on, COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE ar.status = 'submitted') AS unmarked, COUNT(*) AS results FROM bus_assessment a JOIN bus_class_section sec ON sec.id::text = a.class_section_id JOIN bus_course c ON c.id::text = sec.course_id JOIN bus_assessment_result ar ON ar.assessment_id = a.id::text AND ar.deleted_at IS NULL WHERE a.deleted_at IS NULL AND a.status IN ('published', 'marking') GROUP BY a.id, c.name, sec.code, a.title, a.due_on HAVING COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE ar.status = 'submitted') > 0 ORDER BY a.due_on
    %%report teacher-students-below-floor title: Students in my groups below the attendance floor entity: Enrollment help: The pastoral conversation a teacher is expected to have first, and the evidence for it. Below ninety percent a student is missing one lesson in ten, which is a grade, and the teacher sees it before the year head does. sql: SELECT s.student_number, s.first_name || ' ' || s.last_name AS student, c.name AS course, sec.code AS section, e.attendance_rate FROM bus_enrollment e JOIN bus_student s ON s.id::text = e.student_id JOIN bus_class_section sec ON sec.id::text = e.class_section_id JOIN bus_course c ON c.id::text = sec.course_id WHERE e.deleted_at IS NULL AND e.status = 'enrolled' AND e.attendance_rate < 90 ORDER BY e.attendance_rate
    %%report teacher-upcoming-assessments title: Work due in the next fortnight entity: Assessment help: What a teacher checks before setting anything else, and what a head of department reads to see whether a group has four papers in one week. sql: SELECT c.name AS course, sec.code AS section, a.title, a.assessment_type, a.due_on, a.weight_percent FROM bus_assessment a JOIN bus_class_section sec ON sec.id::text = a.class_section_id JOIN bus_course c ON c.id::text = sec.course_id WHERE a.deleted_at IS NULL AND a.status IN ('draft', 'published') AND a.due_on BETWEEN now()::date AND now()::date + 14 ORDER BY a.due_on

%% -- head of department: the subject, and the people teaching it -------------
    %%report hod-results-by-course title: Average score by course entity: Course chart: bar x: course y: average_pct help: What the head of department is asked for at every review. Marks as a percentage of each paper's own maximum, so a course marked out of 40 and one marked out of 100 can sit in the same chart. sql: SELECT c.name AS course, COUNT(ar.id) AS marks, ROUND(AVG(100.0 * ar.score / NULLIF(ar.max_score, 0)), 1) AS average_pct FROM bus_assessment_result ar JOIN bus_assessment a ON a.id::text = ar.assessment_id JOIN bus_class_section sec ON sec.id::text = a.class_section_id JOIN bus_course c ON c.id::text = sec.course_id WHERE ar.deleted_at IS NULL AND a.deleted_at IS NULL AND ar.status = 'marked' AND ar.score IS NOT NULL GROUP BY c.id, c.name ORDER BY average_pct
    %%report hod-marking-turnaround title: How long marking takes, by teacher entity: Staff chart: bar x: teacher y: median_days help: The number a department is actually held to. Days from the due date to the mark being recorded; a teacher consistently at three weeks is not lazy, they are teaching too many groups, and this is the evidence for saying so. sql: SELECT st.first_name || ' ' || st.last_name AS teacher, COUNT(*) AS marked, ROUND(AVG(EXTRACT(EPOCH FROM ar.marked_at - a.due_on::timestamp) / 86400)::numeric, 1) AS median_days FROM bus_assessment_result ar JOIN bus_assessment a ON a.id::text = ar.assessment_id JOIN bus_staff st ON st.id::text = ar.marked_by_id WHERE ar.deleted_at IS NULL AND a.deleted_at IS NULL AND ar.status = 'marked' AND ar.marked_at IS NOT NULL GROUP BY st.id, st.first_name, st.last_name ORDER BY median_days DESC
    %%report hod-weights-not-adding-up title: Groups whose assessment weights do not total 100 entity: ClassSection help: A section whose published papers add to eighty percent has a grade that means nothing, and no diagnostic anywhere reports it. Found at term end it is a re-grade; found in week three it is one edit. sql: SELECT sec.code AS section, c.name AS course, COUNT(a.id) AS papers, SUM(a.weight_percent) AS total_weight FROM bus_class_section sec JOIN bus_course c ON c.id::text = sec.course_id JOIN bus_assessment a ON a.class_section_id = sec.id::text AND a.deleted_at IS NULL AND a.status <> 'cancelled' WHERE sec.deleted_at IS NULL AND sec.status IN ('open', 'in_progress') GROUP BY sec.id, sec.code, c.name HAVING SUM(a.weight_percent) <> 100 ORDER BY ABS(SUM(a.weight_percent) - 100) DESC
    %%report hod-teaching-load title: Teaching load, by teacher entity: Staff chart: bar x: teacher y: students help: What a head of department takes into a timetabling meeting. Groups and students carried, because two teachers with four sections each are not carrying the same load if one of them has forty more children. sql: SELECT st.first_name || ' ' || st.last_name AS teacher, d.name AS department, COUNT(DISTINCT sec.id) AS sections, COUNT(e.id) AS students FROM bus_staff st LEFT JOIN bus_department d ON d.id::text = st.department_id LEFT JOIN bus_class_section sec ON sec.staff_id = st.id::text AND sec.deleted_at IS NULL AND sec.status IN ('open', 'in_progress') LEFT JOIN bus_enrollment e ON e.class_section_id = sec.id::text AND e.deleted_at IS NULL AND e.status = 'enrolled' WHERE st.deleted_at IS NULL AND st.staff_type = 'teaching' AND st.status = 'active' GROUP BY st.id, st.first_name, st.last_name, d.name ORDER BY students DESC

%% -- admissions officer: turning enquiries into students ---------------------
    %%report admissions-open-applications title: Applications waiting on us entity: AdmissionApplication help: The admissions queue, oldest first, because families judge a school by how long it took to answer. Anything past ten working days is a complaint waiting to be made. sql: SELECT ap.reference, ap.applicant_first_name || ' ' || ap.applicant_last_name AS applicant, ap.year_group_applied_for AS year_group, ap.admission_band, ap.status, ap.submitted_on, (now()::date - ap.submitted_on) AS days_waiting FROM bus_admission_application ap WHERE ap.deleted_at IS NULL AND ap.status IN ('submitted', 'under_review') ORDER BY ap.submitted_on
    %%report admissions-offers-unanswered title: Offers the family has not answered entity: AdmissionApplication help: An offer nobody chased is a place held for a family who has already accepted somewhere else, and it is held out of the queue for everyone behind them. Two weeks is the point at which a phone call is worth more than a letter. sql: SELECT ap.reference, ap.applicant_first_name || ' ' || ap.applicant_last_name AS applicant, g.first_name || ' ' || g.last_name AS guardian, g.email, g.phone, ap.decided_on, (now()::date - ap.decided_on) AS days_since_offer FROM bus_admission_application ap JOIN bus_guardian g ON g.id::text = ap.guardian_id WHERE ap.deleted_at IS NULL AND ap.status = 'offer_made' AND ap.decided_on < now()::date - 14 ORDER BY ap.decided_on
    %%report admissions-conversion-by-band title: What each band actually converts at entity: AdmissionApplication chart: bar x: band y: accepted help: The weekly question from the head, and the only evidence that the banding rule is doing anything useful. If review converts as well as priority, the bar is in the wrong place. sql: SELECT ap.admission_band AS band, COUNT(*) AS applications, COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE ap.status = 'accepted') AS accepted, ROUND(100.0 * COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE ap.status = 'accepted') / NULLIF(COUNT(*), 0)) AS conversion_pct FROM bus_admission_application ap WHERE ap.deleted_at IS NULL AND ap.admission_band IS NOT NULL GROUP BY ap.admission_band ORDER BY accepted DESC
    %%report admissions-needing-a-person title: Applications the rule could not band entity: AdmissionApplication help: The band the automation deliberately does not decide: something is missing or borderline and a person has to look. Left alone they sit behind every banded application and age quietly. sql: SELECT ap.reference, ap.applicant_first_name || ' ' || ap.applicant_last_name AS applicant, ap.year_group_applied_for AS year_group, ap.prior_attainment_score, ap.has_sibling_enrolled, ap.submitted_on FROM bus_admission_application ap WHERE ap.deleted_at IS NULL AND ap.admission_band = 'review' AND ap.status IN ('submitted', 'under_review') ORDER BY ap.submitted_on

%% -- finance officer: the money -----------------------------------------------
    %%report finance-overdue-invoices title: Invoices past their due date entity: FeeInvoice help: The chase list, and the first screen of the finance day. Sorted by what is owed rather than by age, because one large balance is worth more than ten small ones and the day is not long enough for both. sql: SELECT f.invoice_number, s.first_name || ' ' || s.last_name AS student, t.name AS term, f.due_on, f.total_amount, f.amount_paid, f.balance_due FROM bus_fee_invoice f JOIN bus_student s ON s.id::text = f.student_id JOIN bus_academic_term t ON t.id::text = f.academic_term_id WHERE f.deleted_at IS NULL AND f.status IN ('issued', 'part_paid', 'overdue') AND f.due_on < now()::date AND f.balance_due > 0 ORDER BY f.balance_due DESC
    %%report finance-debt-ageing title: Outstanding fees by age entity: FeeInvoice chart: bar x: bucket y: outstanding help: What the bursar takes to the governors. Anything past ninety days is a provision decision rather than a chase, and the shape of this chart is what says whether the school has a collection problem or a calendar problem. sql: SELECT CASE WHEN now()::date - f.due_on <= 30 THEN '0-30 days' WHEN now()::date - f.due_on <= 60 THEN '31-60 days' WHEN now()::date - f.due_on <= 90 THEN '61-90 days' ELSE 'over 90 days' END AS bucket, COUNT(*) AS invoices, SUM(f.balance_due) AS outstanding FROM bus_fee_invoice f WHERE f.deleted_at IS NULL AND f.status IN ('issued', 'part_paid', 'overdue') AND f.balance_due > 0 AND f.due_on < now()::date GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
    %%report finance-issued-without-payment title: Issued invoices with no payment at all entity: FeeInvoice help: Not a late payer but a family who has paid nothing since the invoice went out, which is usually a statement that never arrived or a bursary that was agreed and never applied. Both are fixed with one phone call and neither is visible from the ageing report. sql: SELECT f.invoice_number, s.first_name || ' ' || s.last_name AS student, g.email AS billing_email, f.issued_on, f.total_amount FROM bus_fee_invoice f JOIN bus_student s ON s.id::text = f.student_id LEFT JOIN bus_student_guardian sg ON sg.student_id = s.id::text AND sg.deleted_at IS NULL AND sg.is_primary_contact = true LEFT JOIN bus_guardian g ON g.id::text = sg.guardian_id LEFT JOIN bus_payment p ON p.fee_invoice_id = f.id::text AND p.deleted_at IS NULL WHERE f.deleted_at IS NULL AND f.status IN ('issued', 'overdue') GROUP BY f.id, f.invoice_number, s.first_name, s.last_name, g.email, f.issued_on, f.total_amount HAVING COUNT(p.id) = 0 ORDER BY f.issued_on
    %%report finance-daily-takings title: Money received, by month and method entity: Payment chart: line x: month y: received help: The reconciliation the office runs against the bank statement, and the only report here a bank would recognise. Taken from payments received rather than invoices raised, so an unpaid invoice never counts as income. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', p.received_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, SUM(p.amount) AS received, COUNT(*) AS payments FROM bus_payment p WHERE p.deleted_at IS NULL AND p.received_at > now() - interval '12 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
    %%report finance-cancelled-invoices title: Fees written off, and why entity: FeeInvoice help: Every cancelled invoice is money the school chose not to collect, and the reason is free text because the judgement is human. Read together they show whether write-offs are policy or habit. sql: SELECT f.invoice_number, s.first_name || ' ' || s.last_name AS student, t.name AS term, f.total_amount, f.cancellation_reason, f.updated_at FROM bus_fee_invoice f JOIN bus_student s ON s.id::text = f.student_id JOIN bus_academic_term t ON t.id::text = f.academic_term_id WHERE f.deleted_at IS NULL AND f.status = 'cancelled' ORDER BY f.updated_at DESC
    %%report finance-drafts-past-census title: Draft invoices for a term already counted entity: FeeInvoice help: The report that rots silently, and the most expensive one here. The census date passed, the student is being taught, and the invoice was never issued — so nobody is chasing a bill that does not exist. sql: SELECT f.invoice_number, s.first_name || ' ' || s.last_name AS student, t.name AS term, t.census_on, f.total_amount FROM bus_fee_invoice f JOIN bus_student s ON s.id::text = f.student_id JOIN bus_academic_term t ON t.id::text = f.academic_term_id WHERE f.deleted_at IS NULL AND f.status = 'draft' AND t.census_on < now()::date ORDER BY t.census_on
    %%report finance-unapplied-payments title: Payments that did not move the invoice entity: Payment help: A payment recorded against an invoice that is still showing the same balance means the settlement workflow did not run. The money is in the bank and the family is still on the chase list, which is the worst of both. sql: SELECT p.reference, s.first_name || ' ' || s.last_name AS student, f.invoice_number, p.amount, p.balance_before, f.balance_due, p.received_at FROM bus_payment p JOIN bus_fee_invoice f ON f.id::text = p.fee_invoice_id JOIN bus_student s ON s.id::text = f.student_id WHERE p.deleted_at IS NULL AND f.deleted_at IS NULL AND f.status IN ('issued', 'overdue') AND f.balance_due = p.balance_before ORDER BY p.received_at DESC

%% -- counsellor: the children who need somebody to notice --------------------
    %%report counsellor-open-incidents title: Conduct records still open entity: DisciplineIncident help: The pastoral workload, and the list the team works down every morning. Ageing rather than severity, because a minor incident nobody closed for a month is its own kind of failure. sql: SELECT i.reference, s.first_name || ' ' || s.last_name AS student, s.year_group, i.category, i.severity, i.status, i.occurred_at, EXTRACT(DAY FROM now() - i.occurred_at)::int AS days_open FROM bus_discipline_incident i JOIN bus_student s ON s.id::text = i.student_id WHERE i.deleted_at IS NULL AND i.status NOT IN ('closed', 'dismissed') ORDER BY i.occurred_at
    %%report counsellor-repeat-incidents title: Students with a pattern, not an incident entity: Student chart: bar x: student y: incidents help: Three records in a term is a child in trouble rather than a child misbehaving, and it is the point at which the response should change. Nobody sees the pattern from the individual records, which is why this report exists. sql: SELECT s.first_name || ' ' || s.last_name AS student, s.year_group, COUNT(*) AS incidents, MAX(i.occurred_at) AS most_recent FROM bus_discipline_incident i JOIN bus_student s ON s.id::text = i.student_id WHERE i.deleted_at IS NULL AND i.occurred_at > now() - interval '90 days' GROUP BY s.id, s.first_name, s.last_name, s.year_group HAVING COUNT(*) >= 3 ORDER BY incidents DESC
    %%report counsellor-current-suspensions title: Students currently suspended entity: Student help: Who is out of lessons today, and on what authority. A suspension with no incident carrying a suspension sanction is either a keying error or a decision taken outside the process, and both need finding. sql: SELECT s.student_number, s.first_name || ' ' || s.last_name AS student, s.year_group, i.reference AS incident, i.sanction_notes, i.occurred_at FROM bus_student s LEFT JOIN bus_discipline_incident i ON i.student_id = s.id::text AND i.deleted_at IS NULL AND i.sanction = 'suspension' WHERE s.deleted_at IS NULL AND s.status = 'suspended' ORDER BY i.occurred_at DESC NULLS FIRST
    %%report counsellor-unauthorised-absence title: Unauthorised absence, worst first entity: AttendanceRecord chart: bar x: student y: sessions_missed help: The statutory conversation, and the one that reaches a family fastest. An unauthorised absence is the school saying it did not accept the reason, so a run of them is a safeguarding question rather than an attendance one. sql: SELECT s.first_name || ' ' || s.last_name AS student, s.year_group, COUNT(*) AS sessions_missed FROM bus_attendance_record ar JOIN bus_student s ON s.id::text = ar.student_id JOIN bus_class_session ses ON ses.id::text = ar.class_session_id WHERE ar.deleted_at IS NULL AND ses.deleted_at IS NULL AND ar.status = 'absent' AND ar.is_authorised = false AND ses.starts_at > now() - interval '60 days' GROUP BY s.id, s.first_name, s.last_name, s.year_group ORDER BY sessions_missed DESC

%% -- guardian: their own child ------------------------------------------------
    %%report guardian-child-timetable title: My child's groups this term entity: Enrollment help: What a guardian opens the application for, and what stops the phone call to the office. Subject, teacher, day and period, in the order the week runs. sql: SELECT s.first_name || ' ' || s.last_name AS student, c.name AS course, st.first_name || ' ' || st.last_name AS teacher, sec.day_of_week, sec.period, r.code AS room FROM bus_enrollment e JOIN bus_student s ON s.id::text = e.student_id JOIN bus_class_section sec ON sec.id::text = e.class_section_id JOIN bus_course c ON c.id::text = sec.course_id LEFT JOIN bus_staff st ON st.id::text = sec.staff_id LEFT JOIN bus_room r ON r.id::text = sec.room_id WHERE e.deleted_at IS NULL AND e.status = 'enrolled' AND sec.status IN ('open', 'in_progress') ORDER BY s.last_name, sec.day_of_week, sec.period
    %%report guardian-child-attendance title: My child's attendance, by subject entity: Enrollment help: The number the school will quote in any conversation about progress, shown before that conversation rather than during it. A subject twenty points below the others is a timetable problem or a teacher problem, and either is worth asking about. sql: SELECT s.first_name || ' ' || s.last_name AS student, c.name AS course, e.attendance_rate FROM bus_enrollment e JOIN bus_student s ON s.id::text = e.student_id JOIN bus_class_section sec ON sec.id::text = e.class_section_id JOIN bus_course c ON c.id::text = sec.course_id WHERE e.deleted_at IS NULL AND e.status = 'enrolled' ORDER BY s.last_name, e.attendance_rate
    %%report guardian-child-results title: My child's marked work entity: AssessmentResult help: Marks as they were given, with the paper's own maximum beside them, because a 34 means nothing until you know it was out of 40. Newest first, which is the order a family reads them in. sql: SELECT s.first_name || ' ' || s.last_name AS student, c.name AS course, a.title, ar.score, ar.max_score, ROUND(100.0 * ar.score / NULLIF(ar.max_score, 0)) AS percent, ar.marked_at FROM bus_assessment_result ar JOIN bus_assessment a ON a.id::text = ar.assessment_id JOIN bus_class_section sec ON sec.id::text = a.class_section_id JOIN bus_course c ON c.id::text = sec.course_id JOIN bus_student s ON s.id::text = ar.student_id WHERE ar.deleted_at IS NULL AND a.deleted_at IS NULL AND ar.status = 'marked' ORDER BY ar.marked_at DESC
    %%report guardian-outstanding-fees title: What I still owe, and by when entity: FeeInvoice help: One row per unpaid invoice with the balance and the due date, so a family can see what is outstanding without ringing the office — which is most of what the office is rung about. sql: SELECT s.first_name || ' ' || s.last_name AS student, f.invoice_number, t.name AS term, f.due_on, f.total_amount, f.amount_paid, f.balance_due, f.status FROM bus_fee_invoice f JOIN bus_student s ON s.id::text = f.student_id JOIN bus_academic_term t ON t.id::text = f.academic_term_id WHERE f.deleted_at IS NULL AND f.status IN ('issued', 'part_paid', 'overdue') AND f.balance_due > 0 ORDER BY f.due_on

%% ---- Business rules — admission assessment (decides only, cannot act) -------
%% This section carries a node graph and no %%action directives, deliberately.
%% It is the judgement an admissions officer exercises today, written down so it
%% is visible in the application's rule screen and in the viewers — and per §3.4
%% a node-graph rule carries no outputs, so it decides and never writes. The
%% banding it describes is applied by the decision table in the next section.
%%meta name: Admission Assessment
%%meta kind: rules
%%rule admissionAssessment on AdmissionApplication event: beforeCreate priority: 5
flowchart TD
    A([Application received]) --> B{Prior attainment recorded?}
    B -->|No| R1[Send to review: nothing to assess on]
    B -->|Yes| C{Sibling already enrolled?}
    C -->|Yes| P1[Priority: sibling policy]
    C -->|No| D{Attainment at or above the bar?}
    D -->|Yes| P2[Priority: meets the academic bar]
    D -->|No| S1[Standard offer queue]
    R1 --> E([Assessed])
    P1 --> E
    P2 --> E
    S1 --> E

%% ---- Business rules — admission banding (acts: stamps the band) ------------
%%meta name: Admission Banding
%%meta kind: rules
%%rule admissionBanding on AdmissionApplication event: beforeCreate priority: 10
flowchart TD
    A([Application received]) --> B{Attainment recorded?}
    B -->|No| R[Band: review]
    B -->|Yes| C{Sibling enrolled, or at the bar?}
    C -->|Yes| P[Band: priority]
    C -->|No| S[Band: standard]
    R --> E([Banded])
    P --> E
    S --> E

    %%action bandOnSibling transform when: has_sibling_enrolled == true field: admission_band value: priority
    %%action bandOnAttainment transform when: has_sibling_enrolled == false and prior_attainment_score >= 70 field: admission_band value: priority
    %%action bandStandard transform when: has_sibling_enrolled == false and prior_attainment_score < 70 field: admission_band value: standard
    %%action bandForReview transform when: prior_attainment_score == null field: admission_band value: review
    %%action requireDecisionNotesOnRejection validation-error when: status == "rejected" and decision_notes == null message: A rejected application needs a note — it is what the appeal is answered from.
    %%action enrolOnAcceptance trigger-workflow when: status == "accepted" workflow: AdmissionToEnrolment

%% ---- Business rules — the student record ----------------------------------
%%meta name: Student Record Control
%%meta kind: rules
%%rule studentRecordControl on Student event: beforeUpdate priority: 10
flowchart TD
    A([Student record written]) --> B{Leaving?}
    B -->|Yes| C{Date and reason recorded?}
    C -->|No| R1[Refuse: an unexplained leaver cannot be reported]
    C -->|Yes| P[Accept]
    B -->|No| P
    R1 --> E([End])
    P --> E

    %%action requireWithdrawalReason validation-error when: status == "withdrawn" and withdrawal_reason == null message: A withdrawal needs a reason — the retention report is built from it.
    %%action requireWithdrawalDate validation-error when: status == "withdrawn" and withdrawn_on == null message: A withdrawal needs the date the student left.

%% ---- Business rules — enrolment -------------------------------------------
%%meta name: Enrolment Control
%%meta kind: rules
%%rule enrolmentControl on Enrollment event: beforeUpdate priority: 10
flowchart TD
    A([Enrolment written]) --> B{Withdrawing?}
    B -->|Yes| C{Reason given?}
    C -->|No| R1[Refuse]
    C -->|Yes| P[Accept]
    B -->|No| D{Grade recorded before completion?}
    D -->|Yes| R2[Refuse]
    D -->|No| P
    R1 --> E([End])
    R2 --> E
    P --> E

    %%action requireEnrolmentWithdrawalReason validation-error when: status == "withdrawn" and withdrawal_reason == null message: A student leaving a group needs a reason — the subject-change reports are built from it.
    %%action refuseGradeBeforeCompletion validation-error when: status == "pending" and final_grade != null message: A final grade cannot be recorded on an enrolment that has not been placed yet.
    %%action requireGradeOnCompletion validation-error when: status == "completed" and final_grade == null message: A completed enrolment needs a final grade.

%% ---- Business rules — the register ----------------------------------------
%%meta name: Attendance Marking
%%meta kind: rules
%%rule attendanceMarking on AttendanceRecord event: beforeCreate priority: 10
flowchart TD
    A([Mark entered]) --> B{Absent or excused?}
    B -->|Yes| C{Reason recorded?}
    C -->|No| R1[Refuse: the statutory return needs it]
    C -->|Yes| P[Accept]
    B -->|No| D{Late?}
    D -->|Yes| F{Minutes recorded?}
    F -->|No| R2[Refuse]
    F -->|Yes| P
    D -->|No| P
    R1 --> E([End])
    R2 --> E
    P --> E

    %%action requireAuthorisedAbsenceReason validation-error when: status == "absent" and is_authorised == true and absence_reason == null message: An authorised absence needs the reason the school accepted — it is what the inspector asks about.
    %%action requireExcusedReason validation-error when: status == "excused" and absence_reason == null message: An excused mark needs to say what the student was doing instead.
    %%action requireMinutesLate validation-error when: status == "late" and minutes_late == null message: A late mark needs the minutes — the persistent-lateness report sums them.
    %%action clearAuthorisationWhenPresent transform when: status == "present" field: is_authorised value: false

%% ---- Business rules — marking ---------------------------------------------
%%meta name: Marking Control
%%meta kind: rules
%%rule markingControl on AssessmentResult event: beforeUpdate priority: 10
flowchart TD
    A([Mark recorded]) --> B{Score within the paper's maximum?}
    B -->|No| R1[Refuse: a keying error, always]
    B -->|Yes| C{Marked without a score?}
    C -->|Yes| R2[Refuse]
    C -->|No| P[Accept]
    R1 --> E([End])
    R2 --> E
    P --> E

    %%action refuseScoreAboveMaximum validation-error when: score > max_score message: A score cannot exceed the paper's maximum as it stood when the result was created.
    %%action refuseNegativeScore validation-error when: score < 0 message: A score cannot be negative. A missing piece of work is the missing status, not a negative mark.
    %%action requireScoreWhenMarked validation-error when: status == "marked" and score == null message: A marked result needs a score. A blank is not a zero and the reports keep the two apart.

%% ---- Business rules — invoicing -------------------------------------------
%%meta name: Invoice Control
%%meta kind: rules
%%rule invoiceControl on FeeInvoice event: beforeUpdate priority: 10
flowchart TD
    A([Invoice written]) --> B{Cancelling?}
    B -->|Yes| C{Reason recorded?}
    C -->|No| R1[Refuse: every write-off is looked at]
    C -->|Yes| P[Accept]
    B -->|No| D{Issuing?}
    D -->|Yes| F{Issue date set?}
    F -->|No| R2[Refuse]
    F -->|Yes| P
    D -->|No| P
    R1 --> E([End])
    R2 --> E
    P --> E

    %%action requireInvoiceCancellationReason validation-error when: status == "cancelled" and cancellation_reason == null message: A cancelled invoice is money the school chose not to collect — every one of them needs a reason.
    %%action requireIssueDate validation-error when: status == "issued" and issued_on == null message: An issued invoice needs its issue date — the due date and every reminder are measured from it.

%% ---- Business rules — taking money ----------------------------------------
%%meta name: Payment Acceptance
%%meta kind: rules
%%rule paymentAcceptance on Payment event: beforeCreate priority: 10
flowchart TD
    A([Payment offered]) --> B{More than the invoice owes?}
    B -->|Yes| R1[Refuse: a keying error or a credit decision]
    B -->|No| C{Settles the balance?}
    C -->|Yes| S[Settle the invoice]
    C -->|No| T[Post a part payment]
    R1 --> E([End])
    S --> E
    T --> E

    %%action refuseOverpayment validation-error when: amount > balance_before message: A payment cannot exceed what the invoice still owes. A credit is a decision for the finance office, not a keying accident.
    %%action refuseNonPositivePayment validation-error when: amount <= 0 message: A payment must be a positive sum. A correction is a second, offsetting record.
    %%action settleInvoice trigger-workflow when: amount >= balance_before workflow: InvoiceSettlement
    %%action postPartPayment trigger-workflow when: amount < balance_before workflow: PartPaymentPosting

%% ---- Business rules — the timetable ---------------------------------------
%%meta name: Section Control
%%meta kind: rules
%%rule sectionControl on ClassSection event: beforeUpdate priority: 10
flowchart TD
    A([Section written]) --> B{Cancelling?}
    B -->|Yes| C{Reason recorded?}
    C -->|No| R1[Refuse]
    C -->|Yes| W[Withdraw every enrolment on it]
    B -->|No| P[Accept]
    R1 --> E([End])
    W --> E
    P --> E

    %%action requireSectionCancellationReason validation-error when: status == "cancelled" and cancellation_reason == null message: Families are told why a group was pulled, so the reason is written for them and it is required.
    %%action withdrawEnrolmentsOnCancellation trigger-workflow when: status == "cancelled" workflow: SectionCancellation

%% ---- Business rules — conduct ---------------------------------------------
%%meta name: Conduct Outcome
%%meta kind: rules
%%rule conductOutcome on DisciplineIncident event: beforeUpdate priority: 10
flowchart TD
    A([Incident updated]) --> B{Applying a sanction?}
    B -->|Yes| C{Sanction recorded?}
    C -->|No| R1[Refuse: an incident closed with no outcome disappears]
    C -->|Yes| P[Accept]
    B -->|No| D{Closing?}
    D -->|Yes| F{Closure date set?}
    F -->|No| R2[Refuse]
    F -->|Yes| P
    D -->|No| P
    R1 --> E([End])
    R2 --> E
    P --> E

    %%action requireSanction validation-error when: status == "action_taken" and sanction == null message: An incident cannot move to action taken with no sanction recorded — including a sanction of none, which is itself a decision.
    %%action requireSanctionNotes validation-error when: sanction == "suspension" and sanction_notes == null message: A suspension needs its detail — how long, from when, and who agreed it. The appeal is answered from this field.
    %%action requireClosureDate validation-error when: status == "closed" and closed_on == null message: A closed incident needs the date it was closed; the ageing on the open list is measured from it.
    %%action suspendOnSuspension trigger-workflow when: sanction == "suspension" workflow: SuspensionEscalation

